PROJECT is a project directory or its project.kdl. Without one, the
nearest project.kdl at or above the working directory is used.
version prints the SDK, build, compiler and artifact-format identity.
doctor reports the SDK, compiler, player, platform, native backend and,
with --web PLAYER, browser export as supported, unavailable or broken,
changing nothing; it fails only when a capability it checks is broken.
build prepares .chibi/build/game.chibip without starting the player.
check parses, resolves and validates the project as build does, but
migrates and writes nothing; an older project fails until migrated.
test runs each @test function of the packages below ROOT, the
working directory without one, and fails when one fails. ROOT holds
only package files.
fmt rewrites each project's sources and KDL assets as their savers
write them; --check writes nothing and fails when one would change.
A PATH that is a folder without a project.kdl has the package
sources below it formatted instead, as test reads them.
run prepares and starts the player.
Player options are passed to chibi-player; see chibi-player --help.
export compiles the project into DIR with the player, its resources
and engine files, ready to run and ship: a DIR.app on macOS, a
folder with an .exe on Windows, and a folder with a .desktop entry
elsewhere. --web PLAYER writes a static site instead, with the
browser player from the PLAYER folder (make package-web-player).
--archive also writes DIR.tar.gz.
web exports the browser site into a temporary folder, serves it at
http://127.0.0.1:PORT/ (8000 by default; 0 picks a free port) until
interrupted, then removes the folder. Windows does not serve yet.
doc writes the documentation site that ROOT/docs/site.kdl lists, ROOT
being the working directory without one, into ROOT/build/docs;
--serve then serves it like web until interrupted. Windows does not
build documentation yet.
